## Risks and Mitigations (Page 11)

This section identifies potential threats to the testing effort and outlines plans to minimize their impact.

| Risk Description | Probability | Impact | Mitigation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Scope Creep** | Medium | High | Strict adherence to the defined scope. Any new requirements must go through a formal change request process. |
| **Environment Instability** | Medium | Medium | Maintain clear documentation of environment setup. Use automated scripts to minimize manual reconfiguration. Communicate environmental issues immediately. |
| **Defect Backlog** | High | High | Implement daily defect triage meetings. Prioritize defects based on severity and business impact. Ensure a clear definition of "Done." |
| **Resource Constraints** | Low | Medium | Ensure adequate staffing for critical phases. Use automation to increase testing throughput. Prioritize high-risk areas first. |
| **Delayed Fixes** | Medium | Medium | Establish clear SLAs for defect resolution. Escalate unresolved issues to management if timelines are jeopardized. |

